// Input-parser fixture: §7.5's `chars(one_of("^v<>"), skip: whitespace)`
// example, verbatim, at the ROOT over a newline-terminated file.
//
// `skip: whitespace` is horizontal whitespace — spaces and tabs — so it cannot
// absorb the file's trailing `\n`, and it does not have to: the newline is
// whitespace the character parser declined, which is nobody's and not an error.
// The corpus already used this constructor, but only nested inside `sections`,
// whose section regions exclude their line ending — so the one fixture that
// exercised §7.5's example was exactly the shape where the defect was
// invisible.
//
// Reference state: this fixture PASSES on the pre-S20 base b2184c8 and fails
// at 9458fd5. The defect it pins was introduced and closed inside this branch,
// so it is a regression fixture and not a gate for an audit finding.
var moves = read chars(one_of("^v<>"), skip: whitespace);
out(moves.len())
